  Here is a description of the Terraform program that will be defined:

This Terraform program will configure a blue/green deployment with Route53 resources to navigate traffic between Elastic Beanstalk environments. The program will create two Elastic Beanstalk environments, named "blue" and "green", and configure Route53 records to route traffic between the two environments using a weighted routing policy.

Here is the Terraform HCL program:
```
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment" "blue" {
  name = "blue"
  application = "my-app"
  solution_stack_name = "64bit Amazon Linux 2018.03 v2.12.16 running Docker 18.06.1-ce"
  version_label = "my-app-v1"
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment" "green" {
  name = "green"
  application = "my-app"
  solution_stack_name = "64bit Amazon Linux 2018.03 v2.12.16 running Docker 18.06.1-ce"
  version_label = "my-app-v1"
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "blue" {
  name = "blue.my-app.com"
  type = "A"
  zone_id = "Z23ABC4XYZL05B"
  alias {
    name = aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment.blue.endpoint
    zone_id = "Z23ABC4XYZL05B"
    evaluate_target_health = true
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "green" {
  name = "green.my-app.com"
  type = "A"
  zone_id = "Z23ABC4XYZL05B"
  alias {
    name = aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment.green.endpoint
    zone_id = "Z23ABC4XYZL05B"
    evaluate_target_health = true
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "weighted" {
  name = "my-app.com"
  type = "A"
  zone_id = "Z23ABC4XYZL05B"
  set_identifier = "blue-green"
  weighted_routing_policy {
    weight = 50
  }
  set_identifier = "green-blue"
  weighted_routing_policy {
    weight = 50
  }
}
```
This program defines the following resources:

* Two Elastic Beanstalk environments named "blue" and "green"
* Two Route53 records named "blue.my-app.com" and "green.my-app.com"
* A Route53 record named "my-app.com" with a weighted routing policy that routes traffic to the "blue" and "green" environments with a weight of 50% each.

Note that this program assumes that the "my-app" application and the "my-app-v1" version label have already been created in Elastic Beanstalk. If these resources do not exist, you will need to create them before running this program.

