This Terraform program defines an Elastic Beanstalk environment with autoscaling settings using thresholds and CPU utilization, and connects it to a RDS database. It also creates an IAM instance profile and role for the Elastic Beanstalk environment, and grants the necessary permissions to the role to access the RDS database.

Note that this program assumes that the RDS database already exists and is accessible from the Elastic Beanstalk environment. If you need to create the RDS database as part of the Terraform configuration, you can use the `aws_rds_instance` resource to create it.

