  name       = "example_subnet_group"
  subnet_ids = [aws_subnet.private_2.id]
}

resource "aws_security_group" "example" {
  name        = "example_security_group"
  description = "Allow inbound traffic"
  vpc_id      = aws_vpc.example.id

  ingress {
    from_port   = 3306
    to_port     = 3306
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}
```
This Terraform program defines a VPC with three subnets: one public subnet and two private subnets. It also defines an EC2 instance in the public subnet running web servers, an EC2 instance in the private subnet running the application servers, and an RDS instance in the other private subnet serving as the database. The program also defines a security group and a subnet group for the RDS instance.

Note that this is just an example, and you will need to replace the `ami` and `password` values with your own. Additionally, you may need to modify the `instance_type` and `allocated_storage` values to match your needs.

