  To create a SageMaker endpoint using Terraform, you will need to define a `aws_sagemaker_endpoint` resource. Here is an example of how you can do this:
```
resource "aws_sagemaker_endpoint" "example" {
  name = "example-endpoint"
  endpoint_config_name = "example-endpoint-config"
  production_variants {
    variant_name = "example-variant"
    model_name = "example-model"
    initial_instance_count = 1
    instance_type = "ml.m5.large"
  }
}
```
This Terraform configuration will create a SageMaker endpoint named "example-endpoint" with a single production variant named "example-variant" that uses the "example-model" model. The endpoint will be deployed in the "us-west-2" region.

You will also need to define an `aws_sagemaker_endpoint_config` resource to specify the configuration for the endpoint. Here is an example of how you can do this:
```
resource "aws_sagemaker_endpoint_config" "example" {
  name = "example-endpoint-config"
  production_variants {
    variant_name = "example-variant"
    model_name = "example-model"
    initial_instance_count = 1
    instance_type = "ml.m5.large"
  }
}
```
This Terraform configuration will create a SageMaker endpoint configuration named "example-endpoint-config" with a single production variant named "example-variant" that uses the "example-model" model.

You will also need to define an `aws_sagemaker_model` resource to specify the model that will be used by the endpoint. Here is an example of how you can do this:
```
resource "aws_sagemaker_model" "example" {
  name = "example-model"
  primary_container {
    image = "123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/example-model:latest"
    model_data_url = "s3://example-bucket/example-model.tar.gz"
  }
}
```
This Terraform configuration will create a SageMaker model named "example-model" that uses the "example-model.tar.gz" file stored in the "example-bucket" S3 bucket as the model data.

You will also need to define an `aws_s3_bucket` resource to specify the S3 bucket that will be used to store the model data. Here is an example of how you can do this:
```
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "example" {
  bucket = "example-bucket"
  acl    = "private"
}
```
This Terraform configuration will create an S3 bucket named "example-bucket" with private access.

You will also need to define an `aws_iam_role` resource to specify the IAM role that will be used by the endpoint. Here is an example of how you can do this:
```
resource "aws_iam_role" "example" {
  name = "example-role"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "sagemaker.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  })
}
```
This Terraform configuration will create an IAM role named "example-role" that allows the SageMaker service to assume the role.

You will also need to define an `aws_iam_policy` resource to specify the IAM policy that will be used by the endpoint. Here is an example of how you can do this:
```
resource "aws_iam_policy" "example" {
  name = "example-policy"
  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = "sagemaker:*"
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}
```
This Terraform configuration will create an IAM policy named "example-policy" that allows the SageMaker service to perform any action on any resource.

You will also need to define an `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` resource to attach the IAM policy to the IAM role. Here is an example of how you can do this:
```
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "example" {
