  Here is a description of the Terraform program that will be defined:

This Terraform program will create an AWS EC2 instance and configure AWS Backup to back up the instance every day at midnight. The program will also create an IAM role that allows AWS Backup to access the EC2 instance and perform backups.

Here is the Terraform HCL program:
```
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "backup_role" {
  name = "backup_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "backup.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "backup_policy" {
  name = "backup_policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.backup_role.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = "ec2:DescribeInstances"
        Resource = "*"
      },
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = "ec2:CreateTags"
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_ec2_instance" "example" {
  ami           = "ami-12345678"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"

  tags = {
    Name = "example"
  }
}

resource "aws_backup_vault" "example" {
  name = "example"
}

resource "aws_backup_plan" "example" {
  name = "example"
  rule {
    name = "example"
    target_vault = aws_backup_vault.example.id
    schedule = "cron(0 0 * * ? *)"
    lifecycle {
      delete_after = 30
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_backup_selection" "example" {
  name = "example"
  iam_role_arn = aws_iam_role.backup_role.arn
  resources = [aws_ec2_instance.example.arn]
  selection_tag {
    type  = "STRINGEQUALS"
    key   = "Name"
    value = "example"
  }
}
```
This program defines the following resources:

* An AWS IAM role called `backup_role` that allows AWS Backup to access the EC2 instance and perform backups.
* An AWS IAM role policy called `backup_policy` that grants the `backup_role` permission to describe instances and create tags.
* An AWS EC2 instance called `example` that will be backed up by AWS Backup.
* An AWS Backup vault called `example` that will store the backups.
* An AWS Backup plan called `example` that will schedule backups of the `example` EC2 instance every day at midnight.
* An AWS Backup selection called `example` that will select the `example` EC2 instance for backup and apply the `backup_role` IAM role to it.

Note that this program assumes that the `ami-12345678` AMI is available in the `us-east-1` region. If you are using a different region, you will need to modify the `ami` parameter accordingly.

