  Here is a description of the Terraform program I will define:

This Terraform program will create a video streaming site infrastructure using AWS Load Balancing. It will create the following resources:

* An Application Load Balancer (ALB) to distribute incoming traffic across multiple servers
* Two EC2 instances to serve as the backend servers for the ALB
* An IAM role to allow the ALB to access the EC2 instances
* A security group to allow traffic to the ALB and EC2 instances

Here is the Terraform HCL program:
```
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "alb_role" {
  name = "alb_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "elasticloadbalancing.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_security_group" "alb_sg" {
  name        = "alb_sg"
  description = "Security group for the ALB"
  vpc_id      = "vpc-12345678"

  ingress {
    from_port   = 80
    to_port     = 80
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}

resource "aws_alb" "alb" {
  name            = "alb"
  subnets         = ["subnet-12345678", "subnet-87654321"]
  security_groups = [aws_security_group.alb_sg.id]

  access_logs {
    bucket  = "my-alb-logs"
    prefix  = "alb-logs"
    enabled = true
  }
}

resource "aws_instance" "backend_server_1" {
  ami           = "ami-12345678"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"
  subnet_id     = "subnet-12345678"
  vpc_security_group_ids = [aws_security_group.alb_sg.id]
  iam_instance_profile   = aws_iam_role.alb_role.name
}

resource "aws_instance" "backend_server_2" {
  ami           = "ami-12345678"
  instance_type = "t2.micro"
  subnet_id     = "subnet-87654321"
  vpc_security_group_ids = [aws_security_group.alb_sg.id]
  iam_instance_profile   = aws_iam_role.alb_role.name
}
```
This Terraform program will create the following resources:

* An Application Load Balancer (ALB) with two subnets and a security group
* Two EC2 instances to serve as the backend servers for the ALB
* An IAM role to allow the ALB to access the EC2 instances
* A security group to allow traffic to the ALB and EC2 instances

Note that this is just an example configuration and you will need to modify it to fit your specific use case. Additionally, you will need to replace the `vpc-12345678` and `subnet-12345678` with the actual VPC and subnet IDs for your AWS account.

