  Sure, here is a description of the Terraform program I will define:

This Terraform program will create a Load Balancer with an IP Target Group in the specified region. The Load Balancer will be configured with a single listener on port 80 that forwards incoming traffic to the IP Target Group. The IP Target Group will be configured with a single IP address that will be used as the target for the Load Balancer.

Here is the Terraform HCL program:
```
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "example" {
  name               = "example-lb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  security_groups    = [aws_security_group.example.id]
  subnets            = [aws_subnet.example.id]

  listener {
    port     = 80
    protocol = "HTTP"
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_target_group" "example" {
  name     = "example-tg"
  port     = 80
  protocol = "HTTP"
  vpc_id   = aws_vpc.example.id

  health_check {
    path                = "/"
    port                = 80
    protocol            = "HTTP"
    interval            = 30
    timeout             = 5
    healthy_threshold   = 2
    unhealthy_threshold = 2
  }
}

resource "aws_security_group" "example" {
  name        = "example-sg"
  description = "Allow traffic to the example load balancer"
  vpc_id      = aws_vpc.example.id

  ingress {
    from_port   = 80
    to_port     = 80
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}

resource "aws_subnet" "example" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.1.0/24"
  vpc_id     = aws_vpc.example.id
}

resource "aws_vpc" "example" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
}
```
This program defines the following resources:

* `aws_lb`: A Load Balancer with a single listener on port 80 that forwards incoming traffic to the IP Target Group.
* `aws_lb_target_group`: An IP Target Group with a single IP address that will be used as the target for the Load Balancer.
* `aws_security_group`: A Security Group that allows traffic to the Load Balancer on port 80.
* `aws_subnet`: A subnet that will be used by the Load Balancer.
* `aws_vpc`: A VPC that will be used by the Load Balancer and subnet.

Note that this program assumes that you have already created an AWS account and have the necessary credentials to access the AWS API. If you do not have an AWS account, you can create one by visiting the AWS website and following the sign-up process.

