  name = "example"
  port = 80
  protocol = "HTTP"
  vpc_id = aws_vpc.example.id
  target_type = "lambda"
  lambda_function_arn = aws_lambda_function.example.arn
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "example" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.example.arn
  port = 80
  protocol = "HTTP"
  default_action {
    type = "forward"
    target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.example.arn
  }
}
```
This program defines the following resources:

* `aws_lambda_function`: A Lambda function with the specified code and environment variables.
* `aws_lambda_target_group`: A Lambda target group that routes incoming traffic to the Lambda function.
* `aws_lb`: An application load balancer with the specified subnets and security groups.
* `aws_lb_target_group`: An application load balancer target group that routes incoming traffic to the Lambda function.
* `aws_lb_listener`: An application load balancer listener that forwards incoming traffic to the Lambda function.

Note that this program assumes that the Lambda function and load balancer are deployed in the same VPC. If you want to deploy the Lambda function and load balancer in different VPCs, you will need to modify the program accordingly.

